<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakhs give Amoco right to develop two oil fields.</title>
<headline>Kazakhs give Amoco right to develop two oil fields.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan has given Amoco Corp of the United States the right to develop its onshore Temir and Yuzhnaya Emba oil fields, Kazakh Oil head Nurlan Balgimbayev said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Balgimbayev, speaking after a signing ceremony, said Amoco would also be involved in other Kazakh oil projects totalling up to $15 billion over the next two decades.</p>
<p>He gave no details on the two fields.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
